1b749a99449d55d257321321a7bccb33284720f"}},{"id":"559da9bc83bc38fed2aaddfd4c5ded9511d35e96167ea1dc602a32d1d92fcd2f","quote":"Foreign currencies and change in reporting currency","context":"Comprehensive income consists of two components, net income and other comprehensive income, net of tax. Other comprehensive income refers to revenue, expenses, and gains and losses that are recorded as an element of shareholders’ equity but are excluded from net income. The Group’s other comprehensive income consists of foreign currency translation adjustments from its subsidiaries not using the US$ as their functional currency and the fair value change of available-for-sale investments of the Group. Comprehensive income is reported in the consolidated statements of comprehensive income.","section":"Segment reporting","block":1956,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-048127","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001720446","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1720446/000110465926048127/zepp-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c84e76ca59facce479f4f54f81b749a99449d55d257321321a7bccb33284720f.bin","sha256":"c84e76ca59facce479f4f54f81b749a99449d55d257321321a7bccb33284720f"}},{"id":"5396a77b8a4ab717531fc1cfab6dd942416c418054ec010000122978719125c0","quote":"The functional currency and reporting currency of the Company is the US$. The Company’s subsidiaries consolidated VIEs and VIEs’ subsidiaries with operations in the PRC, European subsidiaries and other jurisdictions generally use their respective local currencies as their functional currencies. The financial statements of the Company’s subsidiaries, other than the subsidiaries and consolidated VIEs with the functional currency of US$, are translated into US$ using the exchange rate as of the balance sheet date for assets and liabilities and the average daily exchange rate for each month for income and expense items. Translation gains and losses are recorded in accumulated other comprehensive income or loss as a component of shareholders’ equity.","context":"Foreign currencies and change in reporting currency","section":"Segment reporting","block":1957,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-048127","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001720446","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1720446/000110465926048127/zepp-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c84e76ca59facce479f4f54f81b749a99449d55d257321321a7bccb33284720f.bin","sha256":"c84e76ca59facce479f4f54f81b749a99449d55d257321321a7bccb33284720f"}},{"id":"80c016cc45f9353de55f4eb34ee6a8033d18b368d33f5c04557c18b7ccd538a7","quote":"In the financial statements of the Company’s subsidiaries and consolidated VIEs and VIEs’ subsidiaries, transactions in currencies other than the functional currency are measured and recorded in the functional currency using the exchange rate in effect at the date of the transaction. At the balance sheet date, monetary assets and liabilities that are denominated in currencies other than the functional currency are translated into the functional currency using the exchange rate at the balance sheet date. All gains and losses arising from foreign currency transactions are recorded in the consolidated statements of operations during the year in which they occur. For the years ended December 31, 2023, 2024 and 2025, the transaction gains amounted to US$4,908, US$3,247 and US$2,825 were recorded in general and administrative expenses.","context":"The functional currency and reporting currency of the Company is the US$. The Company’s subsidiaries consolidated VIEs and VIEs’ subsidiaries with operations in the PRC, European subsidiaries and other jurisdictions generally use their respective local currencies as their functional currencies. The financial statements of the Company’s subsidiaries, other than the subsidiaries and consolidated VIEs with the functional currency of US$, are translated into US$ using the exchange rate as of the balance sheet date for assets and liabilities and the average daily exchange rate for each month for income and expense items. Translation gains and losses are recorded in accumulated other comprehensive income or loss as a component of shareholders’ equity.","section":"Segment reporting","block":1958,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-048127","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001720446","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1720446/000110465926048127/zepp-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c84e76ca59facce479f4f54f81b749a99449d55d257321321a7bccb33284720f.bin","sha256":"c84e76ca59facce479f4f54f81b749a99449d55d257321321a7bccb33284720f"}},{"id":"bd5314a0995f9677e82af6715fd310c8e7d17b3e1edf45ce0307bcf0e33802ef","quote":"RMB is not a freely convertible currency. The State Administration for Foreign Exchange, under the authority of the People’s Bank of China, controls the conversion of RMB into other currencies. The value of the RMB is subject to changes in central government policies and to international economic and political developments affecting supply and demand in the China Foreign Exchange Trading System market. The Group’s cash and cash equivalents and restricted cash denominated in US$ and RMB amounted to US$63,001 and US$39,348 as of December 31, 2024, and US$16,627 and US$82,649 as of December 31, 2025, respectively.","context":"In the financial statements of the Company’s subsidiaries and consolidated VIEs and VIEs’ subsidiaries, transactions in currencies other than the functional currency are measured and recorded in the functional currency using the exchange rate in effect at the date of the transaction. At the balance sheet date, monetary assets and liabilities that are denominated in currencies other than the functional currency are translated into the functional currency using the exchange rate at the balance sheet date. All gains and losses arising from foreign currency transactions are recorded in the consolidated statements of operations during the year in which they occur. For the years ended December 31, 2023, 2024 and 2025, the transaction gains amounted to US$4,908, US$3,247 and US$2,825 were recorded in general and administrative expenses.","section":"Segment reporting","block":1959,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-048127","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001720446","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1720446/000110465926048127/zepp-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c84e76ca59facce479f4f54f81b749a99449d55d257321321a7bccb33284720f.bin","sha256":"c84e76ca59facce479f4f54f81b749a99449d55d257321321a7bccb33284720f"}},{"id":"12b65d7605e377c084871f3fe170895cfac1c3ad810b2be7ecc88d2897195c30","quote":"Starting from the second quarter of 2024, the Group changed its reporting currency from RMB to US$, to reduce the impact of increased volatility of the RMB to US$ exchange rate on the Group’s reported operating results. The aligning of the reporting currency with the underlying operations will better depict the Group’s results of operations for each period. The related financial statements prior to April 1, 2024 have been recast to US$ as if the financial statements originally had been presented in US$ since the earliest periods presented. The Group recognized the cumulative foreign currency translation adjustment to the Group’s comprehensive loss amounted to a loss of US$13,620 and US$25,140 for the years ended December 31, 2023 and 2024, respectively.","context":"RMB is not a freely convertible currency. The State Administration for Foreign Exchange, under the authority of the People’s Bank of China, controls the conversion of RMB into other currencies. The value of the RMB is subject to changes in central government policies and to international economic and political developments affecting supply and demand in the China Foreign Exchange Trading System market. The Group’s cash and cash equivalents and restricted cash denominated in US$ and RMB amounted to US$63,001 and US$39,348 as of December 31, 2024, and US$16,627 and US$82,649 as of December 31, 2025, respectively.","section":"Segment reporting","block":1960,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-048127","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001720446","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1720446/000110465926048127/zepp-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c84e76ca59facce479f4f54f81b749a99449d55d257321321a7bccb33284720f.bin","sha256":"c84e76ca59facce479f4f54f81b749a99449d55d257321321a7bccb33284720f"}},{"id":"58dc9f8745af9fd4239357c90843935a5ccc635f111b641d16be3ca4d09bd622","quote":"Basic net income per ordinary share is computed by dividing net income attributable to ordinary shareholders by the weighted average number of ordinary shares outstanding during the period.","context":"Net income per share","section":"Segment reporting","block":1962,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-048127","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001720446","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1720446/000110465926048127/zepp-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/c84e76ca59facce479f4f54f81b749a99449d55d257321321a7bccb33284720f.bin","sha256":"c84e76ca59facce479f4f54f81b749a99449d55d257321321a7bccb33284720f"}},{"id":"0d679e50faed1268e349